Package: qrow
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Query rows in tables, documents and databases from the terminal
 qrow is a fast, keyboard-driven terminal viewer for tabular data, with an
 MCP server that lets AI assistants compute over the same files.
 It supports CSV, TSV, JSON, JSONL, YAML, TOML, Parquet, Arrow, Excel
 (xlsx/xls), SQLite and DuckDB files.  JSON, YAML and TOML open as a table over
 the parsed document, so nested structures can be browsed, edited and converted
 between formats without losing their shape.
 .
 Features include filtering, sorting, pivot tables, computed columns,
 column statistics, histograms and line/bar charts, transposing, and export.
 .
 The package provides two command names: qrow and its short alias qrw.
 It continues tuitab, which stays at 0.11.1; the two install side by side.
